# The build context is the repository root, and COPY source/ takes whatever is
# there — including untracked local files. In CI the checkout is clean, but on a
# developer's machine a scratch database, a .env, or an editor backup under
# source/ would be copied straight into the build stage. This is the only path by
# which anything private could reach a layer.
#
# It also keeps the layer cache from being busted by unrelated local changes.

*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!source/

source/**/*_test.go
source/**/testdata/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/.env
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*~
**/*.swp
